    "script": "scripts/audit-inline-sourcepos.mjs",
    "subject": "Every inline Code and HTML node's position, compared with cmark-gfm's own --sourcepos over the CommonMark spec fixture.",
    "purpose": "Twelve rows, one cause. Our side reports a span that crossed a line ending as though it had not: the start always agrees, the end names a column on the START line that is often past that line's end. adjust_subj_node_newlines (core/inlines.c) is the only code that walks a consumed span's line endings and it is gated behind MARKDOWN_CORE_OPT_SOURCEPOS, which nothing in the tree ever sets. 0a.6 un-gates it. Three of the twelve expect an upstream END COLUMN OF ZERO (1:3..3:0): upstream spells \"the span ends at the line ending\" by naming a column that is not a byte. Agreeing with upstream there will satisfy THIS oracle and leave the row for specs/positions/places.json, which is the intended division of labour and not a contradiction. Only Code and HTML are compared, because upstream carries this repository's autolink, link-start, emphasis-start and consumed-definition position defects too: widening the comparison would make it go red on the commits that fix them.",
